{
  "type": "doc",
  "content": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Logs are usually the first stop in an incident. Yet everyone reading them does not need container command execution; investigation and remediation are often delegated separately."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Part 26 separated Kubernetes configuration reads and changes. Here I separately configured logs and shell on one Pod, testing whether QueryPie could keep logs readable while denying container entry."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Preparing a Pod with Diagnostic Logs"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "In acp-kac-lab, I created orders-diagnostics-demo in orders-lab with fictional order-status logs, not a real service with customer data."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "I created Orders Lab Diagnostics Viewer for Demo Developer. Selecting it and opening Web Client showed the Pod and diagnostics container running normally."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/pod-shell-access/01.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 1. Regular user inspecting lab Pod and container status.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 1. Regular user inspecting lab Pod and container status."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Logs opened directly from Pod details, showing health messages, retries, and completion for fictional DEMO-2901. No shell was needed to inspect events."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/pod-shell-access/02.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 2. Reading fictional order retry and completion messages.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 2. Reading fictional order retry and completion messages."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Establishing a Working Shell Baseline"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Before separating permissions, I allowed both logs and shell in the test role and verified shell connectivity."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Shell opened a terminal. I ran id and printed EP29_QUERYPIE_EXEC_BASELINE_OK, establishing a working baseline before restricting execution, then exited."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/pod-shell-access/03.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 3. Before the policy change, commands execute in the Pod shell.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 3. Before the policy change, commands execute in the Pod shell."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Configuring Logs and Execution Separately"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "In Orders Lab Pod Diagnostics, I retained Pod discovery/details and allowed get on pods/log."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "I denied pods/exec get and create in orders-lab. Even for the same Pod, reading logs and executing commands can be governed separately."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/pod-shell-access/04.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 4. Logs remain Allow; container command execution is Deny.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 4. Logs remain Allow; container command execution is Deny."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Validation found no errors. I saved with a reason; policy v2 was linked to the diagnostic role."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Logs Remain Available, Shell Does Not"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The developer reopened Web Client and the same Pod. Logs still showed health and order-retry events normally."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/pod-shell-access/05.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 5. Logs still work on a new connection after the policy change.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 5. Logs still work on a new connection after the policy change."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Shell now returned Socket connection closed instead of a prompt. The previously working entry route was no longer usable after execution was denied."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/pod-shell-access/06.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 6. Shell connection denied while logs remain permitted.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 6. Shell connection denied while logs remain permitted."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Inspection continued while intervention privileges were managed separately. Delegating troubleshooting did not require giving shell access; operations and development responsibilities could be defined precisely."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Both Allowed Reads and Denied Requests Are Recorded"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Request Audit showed pods/exec, create, DENY, with ‘Denied by policy to access the resource.’ The audit confirmed QueryPie policy caused the rejection."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/pod-shell-access/07.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 7. Shell target, user, role, and policy-denial reason.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 7. Shell target, user, role, and policy-denial reason."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The log read for the same user and role was pods/log, get, ALLOW. Both targeted orders-diagnostics-demo, making permitted and denied operations comparable."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/pod-shell-access/08.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 8. The same Pod’s log read is recorded as ALLOW.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 8. The same Pod’s log read is recorded as ALLOW."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Log-only staff did not need shell privileges. Separating reads and execution on one Pod, with evidence by user and role, was the key benefit: allow necessary inspection and manage direct intervention separately."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The lab used QueryPie Community 11.6.7 Web Client (Beta), a separate K3s cluster, and fictional orders and logs."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
